cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Known Universe
message: If this map or its measurements appear in your work, please cite it with the data build you used (shown in the Data pane and carried in every share link).
type: software
authors:
  - name: blanpa
repository-code: https://github.com/blanpa/known-universe
url: https://blanpa.github.io/known-universe/
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A real-data 3D map of the known universe with a telescope view: Gaia DR3 (positions at the
  Bailer-Jones distances with their errors), HYG placed from DR3 astrometry, the NASA Exoplanet
  Archive, JPL Horizons ephemerides, CDS sky surveys, and live services; cross-identification,
  VOTable export, SAMP, FITS overlays, apparent places, an observer, light-curve period and
  transit search, field diagrams and Galactic orbits. Every astrometric quantity carries its
  uncertainty where the source has one; the maths is checked against astropy, ERFA and JPL.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - Gaia
  - exoplanets
  - sky survey
  - visualization
